# Native client (sfcop --input; oracle/driver/run_native.sh): boot past the key prompt to the main
# menu and click SINGLE PLAYER, which opens Setup (the Single Player screen). Needs a data folder
# with a stored key.
#
# Coordinates are the game's display pixels. The menus run in an 800x600 display mode with the
# 640x480 menu centred, the same space as the Wine driver's client area, so (237, 232) here is
# (237, 232) in skirmish.steps. waitmark is the native player's own: the Wine driver refuses it.

window 60 Starfleet Command

# --- the main menu, "Select Game"
# 60 s until the boot time is fixed: a boot to the menu takes 12 to 23 s here, and the 10 s the
# plan asks for is open (src/app/input/README.md, "Proof runs").
waitmark 60 Select Game
sleep 500

# --- SINGLE PLAYER: Setup, the Single Player screen; a click that does not take fails the run
click 237 232
waitmark 10 Setup
sleep 2000
